  "sport": "basketball",
  "title": "Back up and attack 1v1",
  "description": "Set up a lane of cones about 2 metres wide from half-court to the three-point line. The attacker starts at half-court with the ball and the defender in front. The attacker has to bring the ball up to the three-point line with a control dribble inside the lane while the defender pressures. Dribbling outside the cones is a turnover.\n\nAt the three-point line it becomes live 1v1 to the basket. The attacker must first make at least one and at most two back-up dribbles to create space, then read the defender: if they follow – attack straight past; if they hold back with a shoulder on your middle – drive straight past on that side; if they are square in front – use a change of direction (crossover, behind the back, between the legs or a hesitation). The next pair waits at half-court; switch roles after each go.\n\nProgressions: a narrower lane makes it harder, a wider one easier. Switch hands on the control dribble each time. Then play 2v2 or 3v3 from the same start. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Control dribble: keep the ball low beside your body, with your arm and shoulder protecting it."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Back up with your eyes up – see both the defender and the basket."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Read the defender after the back-up dribble and choose your attack from it."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Defence: pressure without fouling and push the attacker towards the cones."
    }
  ],
